          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The 0-mode of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercharge"} supercharge
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            (an operator in a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+vertex+operator+algebras"}> sheaf of
            )
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triple"} spectral triple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            (see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics#InStringTheory"} there
          %p
            Specifically for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            induced from some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            geometry – such as the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            propagating on that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetimes"} target spacetimes
            – the Dirac-Ramond operator is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} higher analogue
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            on that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            (roughly like what one would expect of a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator+on+a+smooth+loop+space"} Dirac operator on a smooth loop space
            %em Dirac-Ramond operator
            (
            %a{:href => "#Ramond71"}> Ramond 71
            ).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} large volume limit
            of the Dirac-Ramond operator is what is now known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (but in fact the original article
            %a{:href => "#AlvarezKillingbackManganoWindey87"} Alvarez-Killingback-Mangano-Windey 87
            appeared independently and almost in parallel of Witten’s discussion).
