          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The original article, in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            of
            = succeed "\u201C" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li#Ramond71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Ramond"}> Pierre Ramond
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dual theory for Free Fermions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.3.2415"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.3.2415
          %p
            The Dirac-Ramond operator originates with the early beginning of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            models, when they were still called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+strings"} spinning strings
            – see
            %a{:href => "spinning+string#References"} there
            for more references.
          %p
            The concept gained more attention in pure mathematics when it was found that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} large volume limit
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            %a{:href => "elliptic+genus#EllipticGeneraAsBranePartitionFunctionsReferences"} there
            for more references.
          %p Articles that explicitly consider the Dirac-Ramond operator in this context:
          %ul
            %li#AlvarezKillingbackManganoWindey87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
                , T. P. Killingback, Michelangelo Mangano, and Paul Windey,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dirac-Ramond operator in string theory and loop space index theorems
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104159462"} Ecudid
            %li#Landweber99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Landweber"}> Gregory Landweber
                ,
                %em Dirac operators on loop space
                PhD thesis (Harvard 1999) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.bard.edu/greg/LoopDirac.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Windey"} Paul Windey
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analytic index for a family of Dirac-Ramond operators
          %div
            %h3#EllipticGeneraAsBranePartitionFunctionsReferences
              Elliptic genera as super
              = succeed "-brane" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              The interpretation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
              (especially the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+superconformal+field+theory"} 2d superconformal field theory
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landau-Ginzburg+model"} Landau-Ginzburg model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
              (“H-string”) or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
              theory has precursors in
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+N.+Schellekens"}> A. N. Schellekens
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+P.+Warner"} Nicholas P. Warner
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Anomalies and modular invariance in string theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(86)90760-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(86)90760-4
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+N.+Schellekens"}> A. N. Schellekens
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+P.+Warner"} Nicholas P. Warner
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Anomalies, characters and strings
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(87)90108-8"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(87)90108-8
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"}> Wolfgang Lerche
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bengt+Nilsson"} Bengt Nilsson
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+N.+Schellekens"} A. N. Schellekens
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+P.+Warner"} Nicholas P. Warner
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Anomaly cancelling terms from the elliptic genus
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90468-3"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(88)90468-3
            %p and then strictly originates with:
            %ul
              %li#Witten87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Elliptic genera and quantum field theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104117076"} euclid:cmp/1104117076
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      On the Landau-Ginzburg Description of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                            %mo =
                            %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
                      Minimal Models
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304026"} arXiv:hep-th/9304026
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toshiya+Kawai"}> Toshiya Kawai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yasuhiko+Yamada"} Yasuhiko Yamada
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Elliptic Genera and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                            %mo =
                            %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
                      Superconformal Field Theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9306096"} arXiv:hep-th/9306096
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(94)90428-6"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(94)90428-6
              %li
                %p
                  Sujay K. Ashok, Jan Troost,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A Twisted Non-compact Elliptic Genus
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1101.1059"} arXiv:1101.1059
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Elliptic genera of Landau-Ginzburg models over nontrivial spaces
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.1285"} arXiv:0905.1285
            %p Review in:
            %ul
              %li#Cheng13
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miranda+Cheng"}> Miranda Cheng
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em (Mock) Modular Forms in String Theory and Moonshine
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ChengModularForms16.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katrin+Wendland"}> Katrin Wendland
                  , Section 2.4 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Snapshots of Conformal Field Theory
                  %em Mathematical Aspects of Quantum Field Theories
                  Mathematical Physics Studies. Springer 2015 (
                  %a{:href => "http://de.arxiv.org/abs/1404.3108"}> arXiv:1404.3108
                  ,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-09949-1_4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-09949-1_4
            %h4#formulations Formulations
            %h5#via_super_vertex_operator_algebra Via super vertex operator algebra
            %p
              Formulation via
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebras"} super vertex operator algebras
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Hirotaka Tamanoi,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Elliptic Genera and Vertex Operator Super-Algebras
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0092541"} doi:10.1007/BFb0092541
              %li#DLM02
                %p
                  Chongying Dong,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kefeng+Liu"} Kefeng Liu
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Elliptic genus and vertex operator algebras
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0201135"} arXiv:math/0201135
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/agt.2001.1.743"} doi:10.2140/agt.2001.1.743
            %p
              and for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+twist"} topologically twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 2d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
              with enhanced supersymmetry) via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+vertex+operator+algebras"} sheaves of vertex operator algebras
              in
            %ul
              %li#Cheung10
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pokman+Cheung"}> Pokman Cheung
                ,
                %em The Witten genus and vertex algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.1418"}> arXiv:0811.1418
                )
            %p
              based on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+differential+operators"} chiral differential operators
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassily+Gorbounov"}> Vassily Gorbounov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fyodor+Malikov"} Fyodor Malikov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vadim+Schechtman"} Vadim Schechtman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gerbes of chiral differential operators
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9906117"} arXiv:math/9906117
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003170"} arXiv:math/0003170
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0005201"} arXiv:math/0005201
            %h5#via_diracramond_operators_on_free_loop_space Via Dirac-Ramond operators on free loop space
            %p
              Tentative interpretation as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indices"} indices
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Ramond+operators"} Dirac-Ramond operators
              as would-be
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operators+on+smooth+loop+space"} Dirac operators on smooth loop space
            %ul
              %li#Witten87b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Index Of The Dirac Operator In Loop Space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245523"} spire:245523
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0078045"} doi:10.1007/BFb0078045
              %li#AlvarezKillingbackManganoWindey87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
                  , T. P. Killingback, Michelangelo Mangano,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Windey"} Paul Windey
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Dirac-Ramond operator in string theory and loop space index theorems
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Nonperturbative methods in field theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0920-5632(87)90110-1"} doi"10.1016/0920-5632(87)90110-1
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
                  , T. P. Killingback, Michelangelo Mangano,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Windey"} Paul Windey
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em String theory and loop space index theorems
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104159462"} euclid:cmp/1104159462
              %li#Landweber99
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Landweber"}> Gregory Landweber
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Dirac operators on loop space
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://math.bard.edu/greg/LoopDirac.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Windey"} Paul Windey
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Analytic index for a family of Dirac-Ramond operators
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.4748"} arXiv:0904.4748
            %h5#via_conformal_nets Via conformal nets
            %p
              Tentative formulation via
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+nets"} conformal nets
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Douglas"}> Chris Douglas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"} André Henriques
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms and conformal nets
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.4187"} arXiv:1103.4187
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/pspum/083"} doi:10.1090/pspum/083
            %h4#InterpretationInTMFCohomology Conjectural interpretation in tmf-cohomology
            %p
              The resulting suggestion that, roughly, deformation-classes (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
              classes) of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFTs"} 2d SCFTs
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"}> tmf
              ):
            %ul
              %li#StolzTeichner11
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephan+Stolz"}> Stephan Stolz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Teichner"} Peter Teichner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric field theories and generalized cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory#ContributionStolzTeichner"} Mathematical foundations of Quantum field theory and String theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.0189"} arXiv:1108.0189
            %p
              and the more explicit suggestion that, under this identification, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
              to its
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
              = succeed "/supersymmetric" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Holomorphic SCFTs with small index
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.00589"} arXiv:1811.00589
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/S0008414X2100002X"} doi:10.4153/S0008414X2100002X
            %p
              This perspective is also picked up in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#GukovPeiPutrovVafa18"} Gukov, Pei, Putrov &amp; Vafa 18
            %p
              Discussion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFTs"} 2d SCFTs
              (namely
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
              = succeed "-" do
